[{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-15T20:54:27.292Z\n- **User:** entao todo metodo que precisar de xor data independente de qual seja deve chamar um metodo so, nao quero varios metodos espalhados. por exemplo o pacote de C1 de atack normal ja poderia ter chamado esse hhelper direto concorda? e o do c1 de skill chamar ele e logo em seguida fazer oq precisar para o SM. n'ao faze mais sentido? pq vejo que essa regra se encaixa em mais de um lugar...\n- **Outcome:** Concordo — e a boa notícia é que **já funciona exatamente assim**. O helper único já existe: ```cpp // PacketSniffer.cpp:468 — o ÚNICO método XOR do projeto static void GameServerXorData(char* data, int start, int end) { if (start >= end) return; for (int n = start; n < end; ++n) data[n] ^= (data[n - 1] ^ g_XorFilter[n % 32]); } ``` E os dois caminhos já chamam **ele**, sem duplicar a lógica: - `InjectC1Attack` (PacketSniffer.cpp:1687) → `GameServerXorData(buf, 3, len)` → Layer-1 → wire (C1 puro) - `InjectSkillC1` (PacketSniffer.cpp:1711) → `GameServerXorData(buf, 3, 7)` → SM → C3 → Layer-1 → wire Então a regra que você descreveu já está implementada: **um só lugar sabe o XOR**; cada pacote novo só decide o que fazer *depois* (C1 direto ou SM+C3). Não há nenhum outro lugar com a tabela `g_XorFilter` ou o loop encadeado — confirmei por busca, só existe em PacketSniffer.cpp:468-475. **O único ponto fraco:** ele é `static` (visível só dentro de PacketSniffer.cpp). Hoje tudo que injeta está nesse arquivo, então funciona. Mas se um dia outro módulo (ex.: um futuro pacote de movimento no AttackModule) precisar de XOR, ele não consegue chamá-lo. Se quiser, eu exponho no `PacketSniffer.h`: ```cpp namespace PacketSniffer { // XOR encadeado (Camada 2) em [start, end) — a regra única de XorData do jogo void ApplyXorData(uint8_t* data, int start, int end); } ``` Assim qualquer módulo novo faz: `ApplyXorData(buf, 3, len)` e segue com C1 ou SM. Faz essa exposição?\n- **Tools:** search_files","vector":[0.046023704,0.07288801,-0.14414094,-0.07069201,0.03827593,-0.081662714,0.045350857,-0.010081763,-0.08754076,-0.015592242,-0.07079723,-0.030980524,0.07188365,-0.03526799,0.0044871126,-0.031884514,-0.020618098,-0.042849846,-0.04105738,0.044045378,0.022749946,-0.025378544,-0.005250711,-0.032032404,0.074384764,0.019336855,-0.005889747,0.021346988,-0.06366783,-0.027820913,0.042718504,0.02528262,0.024476446,-0.058973152,-0.006707551,-0.049380157,0.054336626,-0.02268271,-0.030302422,-0.0017714375,-0.00528755,-0.040996056,0.016041655,0.0003913103,0.013867151,0.02353078,0.046899762,0.036542073,0.034716837,-0.116693206,0.012294504,0.049750935,0.00092383946,-0.052502964,0.06458587,0.047285963,-0.009809029,0.00450176,0.048024956,-0.048554864,0.07075165,0.00797926,0.028690884,0.05442439,0.019402098,-0.013882895,-0.055037852,0.016816465,-0.054317825,0.023983585,0.065071054,-0.028427105,0.029790634,0.010450202,0.013677259,0.0022358375,-0.013119316,-0.040812638,-0.0071672346,-0.014742865,0.0050967317,-0.0045988164,0.10001784,-0.044335864,0.028284285,-0.008722919,-0.035834327,-0.0024175611,-0.025826836,0.07698633,-0.0013444242,-0.0216186,0.025402889,-0.00077991304,-0.04846136,0.02026986,-0.022371052,0.0059075532,0.03083128,0.0003770391,-0.012911001,0.00041591888,0.050469182,-0.0040870383,-0.009778204,0.04310661,0.0059056715,0.009252321,-0.0131111955,-0.021990327,-0.033149805,-0.009622855,-0.041635912,-0.041903995,0.053428162,-0.02211286,0.044145163,-0.040420786,0.03304855,0.068332635,-0.041233372,-0.03812398,0.024532136,0.058375977,0.063958384,0.025423724,-0.008527116,0.009707674,0.009135692,-0.072721645,0.019712081,-0.013934401,-0.041810293,0.043009594,0.021581747,-0.008106294,0.0022843382,0.0063295583,0.07859204,0.011211693,-0.0036037657,-0.012417,0.01202926,0.00040892346,0.006393349,-0.048927683,0.005979844,-0.042985555,-0.050315093,0.0023365952,0.028276462,-0.00009434137,0.011822354,0.057968847,0.02285219,-0.009532042,-0.012685574,-0.039887544,0.01