,-0.0038929374,0.026349917,-0.063350156,-0.025896238,0.05184469,0.0035351291,-0.0010693651,-0.034114864,0.0001641417,-0.052250344,-0.0222058,-0.03143184,0.034622777,0.03460452,0.009690264,0.026501011,-0.007906053,-0.068975106,-0.010227992,0.017004676,-0.021036224,0.036070846,-0.04033263,-0.061216425,-0.0060774926,0.0050358777,0.014914814,0.022339491,0.0053661717,0.13341446,0.032436468,0.011696006,-0.039948024,0.03803644,0.047098797,0.010847385,-0.03969055,-0.011992928,0.020661395],"hash":"bce7ef10:1780","model":"nomic-embed-text:latest","archived":true},{"uri":"file:///f%3A/blackrockmu/.novamind/memory/session-log.md","text":"## 2026-11-16T02:49:07.104Z\n- **User:** essa era a versao que funcionava.. // ============================================================================ // InjectSkillC1 — Injeta o PLAINTEXT REAL de um skill attack C1 0x19. // Pipeline (diferente do 0x11, que vai C1 puro): // 1. XorData[3,7) — XOR encadeado no payload (key m_XorFilter, anchor 0x19) // 2. SM input — [serial 0x08793700] + payload XorData'd [19 sH sL iH iL] // 3. SimpleModulus — 6 bytes → 11 bytes (1 bloco) // 4. C3 0D [11] — header C3 + size // 5. Layer-1 + send // O …\n- **Outcome:** ## Causa raiz encontrada e corrigida (sem commit, como pediu) ### O que o git mostra | commit | o que fez na skill | |---|---| | `5330bda` (14/11 16:43) | **introduziu o bug real** (clamp do checksum do SM) | | `c6ed86c` (15/11 13:50) | trocou a fila (que usava o **builder nativo do jogo**: `0x404B40/0x404B90/0x4050D0/0x404D70`) pelo pipeline C3+SM reimplementado à mão — **nunca validado em campo** (docs 01/02 ficaram \"Pendente (validação em campo)\") | | `e0945a2` (Fase 0) | removeu a fila do builder como \"código morto\" | | refactor `c92afdc…5becc0a` + auto-potion `964db9d` | **não mudaram os bytes da skill** (comparei linha a linha: idênticos). A única regressão do `964db9d` foi **no log** (passou a imprimir a forma Camada-2 em vez do plaintext) | ### A causa raiz (provada com o log de campo) `SimpleModulusCipher::EncryptBlock` **cifra 8 bytes** do source (o word 3 da chave SM sai dos 2 bytes *além* do buffer de 6 bytes = **lixo de stack**), mas calculava o checksum com **zeros** nesses 2 bytes → o pacote sai **autoinconsistente**. Decifrei o pacote que o bot injetou (18:26:03) com o algoritmo de decifra do byp — validado, porque reproduz `ring`/`finale`/checksum do log **exatamente** nos pacotes nativos: | pacote | checksum do servidor | |---|---| | nativo do jogo `C3 0D 25 8F …` | ✅ `calc=0xBC expected=0xBC` (bytes \"além\" = `61 02`) | | **injetado pelo bot** `C3 0D 8D 1F …` | ❌ **`calc=0x41 expected=0xDF`** → servidor rejeita → **derruba a conexão** | Por isso o **ataque n…\n- **Tools:** tool_search, search_files, edit_file, run_command, repl","vector":[0.057005994,0.06202963,-0.14317277,0.00026382587,0.051593743,-0.06258082,0.05752293,0.026302274,-0.059233755,-0.03257067,-0.07762713,0.020566413,0.08439261,-0.030488107,0.015933039,-0.020892857,-0.007730795,-0.056860384,-0.030397607,0.074701115,0.023844114,-0.03354529,-0.029547244,-0.015593008,0.10611159,0.035010733,-0.02219368,0.037822757,-0.035017613,-0.0038406893,0.027778601,0.0017912865,-0.0035815905,-0.023255233,0.0003759363,-0.0625097,0.025680441,-0.012081068,-0.010297297,-0.015171394,0.0075324792,-0.025389858,-0.009764489,0.010577877,0.019921044,0.041565225,0.035560057,0.030763572,0.06985107,-0.12229236,0.018022768,0.010864455,0.0017772263,-0.055398803,0.07620825,0.029652948,-0.04729799,-0.00918604,0.031112269,-0.036155224,0.05194747,0.015649244,-0.012006656,0.06330473,-0.025039336,-0.01124075,-0.03890093,0.05349818,-0.037536506,-0.0031129092,0.05912281,-0.014688188,0.031187408,0.010733213,-0.01706752,0.0058507347,-0.03876331,-0.03537975,-0.02086983,-0.017656377,0.008832914,0.0037561113,0.09665677,-0.03720924,0.03327751,-0.016059717,-0.055256877,-0.048485033,-0.069534086,0.07249194,-0.0008672705,-0.008971943,0.008091209,-0.005112298,-0.047058675,-0.026270092,-0.058577772,-0.00302545,0.0113953