AL** — 17 no total | | `F3 E5` / `E2` / `FC` / `F1` | posição, alvo, ping — **nada de life** | | `F3 E0` / `E1` / `03` | **não existem** nesse servidor | Sem o máximo, `life/maxLife` dá `-1%` → o limiar nunca era avaliado. Era por isso que o log mostrava `DECISAO: life=202/0 (-1%)`. Confirmei também no source do cliente (`Main_EX603/Main/Protocol.cpp`) que `0xFE` = máximo e `0xFF` = atual (o fix anterior está certo) — e que o **cliente tem o máximo**: `PrintPlayer.cpp` declara os globals da HUD **consecutivos**: ```cpp DWORD ViewIndex, ViewReset, ViewValue, ViewPoint; DWORD ViewCurHP, ViewMaxHP, ViewCurMP, ViewMaxMP; DWORD ViewCurBP, ViewMaxBP, ViewCurSD, ViewMaxSD; ``` ## O que fiz **`src/game/GameMemory/ClientVitals.cpp`** (novo): varre as seções graváveis do `main.exe` procurando esse bloco, usando **4 assinaturas independentes** vindas da rede (life, mana, BP e escudo — o BP é 160 fixo nesse servidor). Quatro valores casando = identificação praticamente única. Depois disso o byp lê o HP/MP **direto do cliente** (sem atraso de rede). **`AutoPotion.cpp`**: os vitais do cliente viram a fonte primária; rede/calc ficaram como …\n- **Tools:** read_file, search_files, write_file, edit_file, run_command, manage_todos","vector":[0.051720217,0.03819617,-0.17333104,-0.03085916,0.04772795,-0.07908049,0.070366725,-0.01002622,-0.06954258,-0.020535344,-0.04721361,-0.000368019,0.03799958,-0.0435201,0.03158594,-0.046616707,-0.015296186,-0.054744177,-0.046686612,0.0051875575,-0.003595939,-0.054193944,0.00096782576,0.010641604,0.07603508,0.050445918,-0.015337223,0.09719044,-0.0491936,-0.028954284,0.035621036,0.040035978,0.0025591129,-0.021437403,-0.014771005,-0.0070748776,0.08749564,0.017490635,0.019365525,-0.028967083,0.013481649,-0.09614587,0.03303119,-0.00798844,0.009491402,-0.027484966,0.040023528,0.018244063,0.05903016,-0.08784291,0.05122,0.019497065,0.018741038,-0.024034174,0.08519935,0.01885669,-0.029695477,0.026557842,-0.0066539375,-0.049901564,0.09114915,0.026157377,0.017